{
  "pedal": "Boss NS-2 Noise Suppressor — the gain read directly: the signal into INPUT, a probe into RETURN (mono: OUTPUT)",
  "comment": "The NS-2's detector listens to INPUT; its gain element sits between RETURN and OUTPUT. The interface's loopback output plays a steady three-tone probe into RETURN (loop_probe), so OUTPUT is the probe times the gate's gain at every instant, however quiet the input. Cabling: interface out 3 to INPUT as always; the loopback cable's far end moves from interface input 5 to the pedal's RETURN (its near end stays in interface out 4); SEND empty; OUTPUT to interface input 2. Each setting has a take of test tones placed around its threshold and a take of guitar (tools/capture/ns2/make_focused_plan.py writes this file and says what is in them). Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise, 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered so each step turns one knob.",
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "marker_to_pedal": false,
  "loop_probe": {
    "freq": [
      1877,
      2341,
      3163
    ],
    "level_db": -12
  },
  "knobs": [
    "Threshold",
    "Decay",
    "Mode"
  ],
